# Handlingar — local secrets (the ONE place all secrets live).
#
# SETUP:  cp .local/.env.example .local/.env   then fill in the values below.
# `.local/.env` is gitignored and must NEVER be committed. Only this .example is tracked.
#
# Consumed automatically by:
#   - the Makefile        (`-include .local/.env`, so every `make` target sees these)
#   - scripts/preflight.sh (validates the token before provisioning)
#
# Format is plain KEY=value (no quotes, no `export`, no spaces around `=`).
# `make preflight` will tell you exactly what's missing if you skip a value.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HCLOUD_TOKEN  —  Hetzner Cloud API token (Read & Write).   REQUIRED.
# Used by: make cluster-up / cluster-down / bringup (cluster provisioning).
# Where to get it:
#   Hetzner Cloud Console  https://console.hetzner.cloud/
#   → select the project   → Security → API tokens → "Generate API token"
#   → permission: Read & Write   → copy the 64-char token (shown only once).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
HCLOUD_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN  —  Cloudflare API token for the handlingar.se zone.  REQUIRED for ingress.
# Used by: make ingress-up (creates the k8s Secret consumed by BOTH
#   cert-manager (Let's Encrypt DNS-01 challenge) and external-dns (auto-manages
#   the dev.handlingar.se A record → load-balancer IP)).
# Where to get it:
#   Cloudflare dashboard  https://dash.cloudflare.com/
#   → My Profile → API Tokens → "Create Token"
#   → use the "Edit zone DNS" template
#   → Permissions:  Zone · DNS · Edit   AND   Zone · Zone · Read
#   → Zone Resources:  Include → Specific zone → handlingar.se   (scope to this zone ONLY)
#   → copy the token (shown only once).
# Least-privilege + single-zone scope is deliberate: this token can edit DNS for
# handlingar.se but nothing else. external-dns is configured upsert-only so it can
# never delete prod records — see infra/k8s/ingress/ and ADR 0006.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DB_PASSWORD  —  Postgres password for the dev app + postgres pod.   OPTIONAL.
# Used by: make deploy / app-up (creates the k8s Secret `alaveteli-secrets`).
# Leave BLANK to have a throwaway dev password auto-generated on first deploy.
# Set a value only if you want a stable/known password (e.g. to psql in by hand).
# Self-generated (internal to the cluster), not retrieved from anywhere.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DB_PASSWORD=
